AArch64: keep a truncating store truncating when its __ptr32 address is widened.

performSTORECombine casts a ptr32 (address space 270/271) base pointer to the default address space and re-creates
the store with DAG.getStore, which stores the whole value operand. After type legalization an i8/i16 store is a
truncating store of an i32 value, so `*(unsigned short *__ptr32)p = v` wrote 4 bytes and cleared the two after it
(seen as the script memory tree losing its free lists: head[n + 1] zeroed by every write to head[n]).

Applies to llvm-project 21.1.8 on top of clang-21-x86_64-ptr32-abi.patch (independent of it).

--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64ISelLowering.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64ISelLowering.cpp
@@ -24002,6 +24002,11 @@
     MVT PtrVT = TLI.getPointerTy(DAG.getDataLayout());
     if (PtrVT != Ptr.getSimpleValueType()) {
       SDValue Cast = DAG.getAddrSpaceCast(DL, PtrVT, Ptr, AddrSpace, 0);
+      if (ST->isTruncatingStore())
+        return DAG.getTruncStore(Chain, DL, Value, Cast, ST->getPointerInfo(),
+                                 MemVT, ST->getBaseAlign(),
+                                 ST->getMemOperand()->getFlags(),
+                                 ST->getAAInfo());
       return DAG.getStore(Chain, DL, Value, Cast, ST->getPointerInfo(),
                           ST->getBaseAlign(), ST->getMemOperand()->getFlags(),
                           ST->getAAInfo());
